    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nvecql4",
      "content": "<img></img>Directive Principles of State Policy (DPSP) are guidelines to the government for creating a just and welfare-oriented society. They are contained in Part IV of the Constitution of India (Articles 36–51). Although they are not enforceable by courts, they are fundamental in the governance of the country."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Constitutional Part",
          "value": "Part IV",
          "icon": "book"
        },
        {
          "label": "Article Range",
          "value": "Articles 36–51",
          "icon": "calendar"
        },
        {
          "label": "Source Country",
          "value": "Irish Constitution",
          "icon": "award"
        },
        {
          "label": "Classifications",
          "value": "3 Categories",
          "icon": "check"
        }
      ],
      "id": "kldy8z7"
    },
    {
      "id": "3wxw83b",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning and Importance of DPSP"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Directive Principles of State Policy are contained in Part IV of the Constitution from Articles 36 to 51.",
        "The concept of DPSP was borrowed from the Irish Constitution of 1937, which derived it from the Spanish Constitution.",
        "DPSPs are non-justiciable in nature, meaning they are not legally enforceable by courts for their violation.",
        "The principles are categorized into Socialist, Gandhian, and Liberal–Intellectual principles.",
        "They aim to establish social and economic democracy and create a welfare state in India."
      ],
      "id": "hdhwyaq"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s90dw0s",
      "content": "• DPSP aim to establish social and economic democracy in India."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3l1te7m",
      "content": "• They guide the government in making laws and policies."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qk00hxs",
      "content": "• They promote welfare of the people."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u3zvzza",
      "content": "• They help in establishing a welfare state."
    },
    {
